    "['test-id [id] mep [mep-id] peer-ip [ip-address]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ethernet cfm maintenance-point mep domain md1 ma ma1 mep 2 remote-mepid 1 continuity-check', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nethernet cfm maintenance-point mep domain md1 ma ma1 mep 2 remote-mepid 1 continuity-check\\nethernet cfm sla test-id 1 mep-id 2 peer 2.2.2.2\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The first Cisco command establishes the CFM MEP configuration with the remote MEP ID.\\n2. The second command creates the SLA test instance with the test ID, local MEP ID, and peer IP address, which is the direct equivalent of Huawei's `test-id 1 mep 2 peer-ip 2.2.2.2`.\\n\\nNote: Cisco's CFM implementation requires these two separate commands to achieve the same functionality as Huawei's single command. The first part establishes the MEP relationship, while the second configures the specific test parameters.\", 'trans_template': 'ethernet cfm maintenance-point mep domain md1 ma ma1 mep 2 remote-mepid 1 continuity-check'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ethernet cfm sla test-id 1 mep-id 2 peer 2.2.2.2', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nethernet cfm maintenance-point mep domain md1 ma ma1 mep 2 remote-mepid 1 continuity-check\\nethernet cfm sla test-id 1 mep-id 2 peer 2.2.2.2\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The first Cisco command establishes the CFM MEP configuration with the remote MEP ID.\\n2. The second command creates the SLA test instance with the test ID, local MEP ID, and peer IP address, which is the direct equivalent of Huawei's `test-id 1 mep 2 peer-ip 2.2.2.2`.\\n\\nNote: Cisco's CFM implementation requires these two separate commands to achieve the same functionality as Huawei's single command. The first part establishes the MEP relationship, while the second configures the specific test parameters.\", 'trans_template': 'ethernet cfm sla test-id 1 mep-id 2 peer 2.2.2.2'}]]": 1,
